ny of these a second time.", "reference": "1873, Old and new - Volume 8, page 101:"}, {"text": "I do not mean to say we have never employed some of them who come to us—but we have never circulared agents or gone after them.", "reference": "1909, American Life Convention, Report of the Proceedings of the Annual Meeting of the American Life Convention, page 42:"}, {"text": "If you've ever been circulared by drug repackaging houses, you know they usually offer to trade a selection of office supplies for your unused drug samples.", "reference": "1962, Harrie Sheridan Baketel, Medical Economics - Volume 39, page 141:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To extend in a circular direction.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The theme can be expressed in an architectural analogy. For, of all contriving to encover space, the arch — alone or 'circulared' into the dome — is the most ingenious.", "reference": "2008, Donald E. Wagner, Kenneth Cragg, Dying in the Land of Promise, page 116:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circular", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}